# Shortfin UI — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local (or .env) for local dev; set in Vercel Project Settings for deploys.

## LOCAL DEV (running `pnpm dev` on your own machine) — set ONLY these:
#
#   API_ORIGIN=https://openclaw.117aub.online/brain-api
#   SESSION_SECRET=<MUST MATCH the server's apps/web/.env value — fetch from the box:
#                  grep SESSION_SECRET /data/workspace/Projects/Hyperliquid/platform/apps/web/.env>
#   ADMIN_ADDRS=<your wallet address, lowercase — routes you to /desk>
#
# Then open http://localhost:3000/platform   (note the /platform basePath in local dev!)
#
# ⚠️ DO NOT set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL locally. It forces the browser to call the
# brain API cross-origin — which breaks wallet auth (auth routes live in the
# web app, and cookies need same-origin). The same-origin rewrites + API_ORIGIN
# handle everything: your dev server proxies API calls to the box. No CORS.

## VERCEL (Production + Preview):
#   API_ORIGIN=https://openclaw.117aub.online/brain-api
#   SESSION_SECRET=<same as the box>
#   ADMIN_ADDRS=<admin wallet(s), comma-separated, lowercase>
# (No NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars needed. basePath auto-detects Vercel = root domain.)

## Optional escape hatch (rarely needed)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL — absolute API base for the browser, bypassing rewrites.
# Only for direct-dev against a local brain API (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8890).

# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID — Reown cloud project id for mobile-wallet
# (WalletConnect) support. OPTIONAL: a working default is compiled in (public
# identifier, not a secret), so nothing to set here unless you swap projects.

# No token belongs in this file: the desk token is entered once in the UI per browser.
